  "summary": "An Ookpik ([ukˈpik]) is a popular Inuit handicraft toy.",
  "description": "An Ookpik ([ukˈpik]) is a popular Inuit handicraft toy. It is a small, souvenir owl with large head and big eyes, a beak, and small black talons. They are often made from wolf fur, sealskin and other traditional materials.\n\nUkpik (ᐅᒃᐱᒃ) is the Inuktitut word for snowy owl.",
